## User question:
How to configure Huawei router's BGP peer group "backbone_peers" to allow the BGP label to use its own QoS priority instead of inheriting from the outer MPLS tunnel label?
---
## Proposed answer:
peer-group backbone_peers
label-policy local-preference
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> exp-mode { pipe | uniform }
undo peer <group-name> exp-mode
FuncDef:
The peer exp-mode command specifies the mode in which a BGP label inherits the QoS priority in the outer tunnel label carried in packets.
The undo peer exp-mode command restores the default mode.

The default QoS priority inheriting mode varies according to the outer MPLS tunnel type:


LDP: By default, the BGP label inherits the QoS priority carried in the outer MPLS tunnel label.

TE: By default, the BGP label does not inherit the QoS priority carried in the outer MPLS tunnel label.

LDP over TE: By default, the BGP label inherits the QoS priority carried in the outer MPLS tunnel label.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a BGP peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'pipe', 'Info': 'Allows the BGP label to use its own QoS priority.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'uniform', 'Info': 'Allows the BGP label to inherit the QoS priority carried in the outer MPLS tunnel label.\n-'}
